title: 'Asset Hub Westend: benchmark XCM fee instructions on the swap trader'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Asset Hub Westend's `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic` worst case for `BuyExecution`, `PayFees`
    and `RefundSurplus` paid fees in the native asset, so it measured the `UsingComponents` trader
    and never the `SwapFirstAssetTrader` that runs when fees come in a foreign asset. That swap
    goes through `pallet_asset_conversion` and costs several times the native path, and the
    runtime charged the native weight for it. `worst_case_for_trader` now pays in a foreign asset
    with a pool against the native asset, sharing the pool setup with `worst_case_asset_exchange`,
    so the swap is what gets measured. The setup also funds the staking pot, so the trader's fee
    settlement is measured as the balance update it is on a live chain rather than as an account
    creation or a burn.

    The `refund_surplus` benchmark buys twice the surplus it then refunds. A trader that swapped
    the fee asset refunds less than it was paid, so refunding the whole purchase refunded nothing
    and the benchmark's assertion failed against such a trader.

    A runtime wiring `SwapFirstAssetTrader` prices the swap only if its own `worst_case_for_trader`
    returns a foreign asset with a pool against the native asset and `worst_case_holding` carries
    that asset; regenerating `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic` alone re-measures `UsingComponents`.
    Runtimes with only `UsingComponents` need no regeneration.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Asset Hub Westend charges `BuyExecution`, `PayFees` and `RefundSurplus` the weight of the swap
    path whatever the fee asset, so messages paying in WND are charged more as well. With this
    runtime's `InMemoryDbWeight`, `BuyExecution` goes from about 28 µs to about 254 µs,
    `PayFees` from about 104 µs to about 330 µs and `RefundSurplus` from about 2 µs to about
    267 µs, each with a proof size of 6196 bytes. Senders with a hard-coded `Limited` weight limit
    covering these instructions may now fail with `Overweight` and should raise it; senders using
    `Unlimited` or `XcmPaymentApi::query_xcm_weight` need no change.
crates:
- name: pallet-xcm-benchmarks
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
